# A config template for paced-series.sh. Copy it to the round's worktree as gitignored
# attic/expNNN/series.env, because the real values are local paths, and fill in every
# placeholder from the round's protocol. The driver sources this file as bash after
# unsetting every key, so a value comes only from here. Quote any value with spaces.
# Check it with:  paced-series.sh --config attic/expNNN/series.env --check
#
# A helper for the paths below, not a key the driver reads: the directory that holds this
# checkout's worktrees and the corpus.
WORKTREES=/path/to/worktrees

# ---- the round
# The round's id, exp-NNN. It is the harness's --exp, names the bench directory
# ($HARNESS_WT/.bench/transitions/$ROUND) and prefixes the files written to OUT.
ROUND=exp-NNN
# The round's worktree, at its top level, and its branch. The protocol is committed here
# and pushed to origin/$BRANCH; the series lock is read from this worktree's git common dir.
WORKTREE=$WORKTREES/metabrowser-perf-expNNN
BRANCH=claude/perf-expNNN
# The protocol, relative to WORKTREE. Its directory, beside the record, must be clean.
PROTOCOL=explorations/performance-loop/experiments/exp-NNN-protocol.txt
# Where the driver writes the power log, the 15 s samples, the judged mode and the pair
# logs. It must be inside WORKTREE and ignored by Git.
OUT=$WORKTREE/attic/expNNN

# ---- the builds: each checkout clean at its full commit, with its `metab --version` line
CONTROL_WT=$WORKTREES/metabrowser-perf-control
CONTROL_HEAD="<40-hex control commit>"
CONTROL_VERSION="<the control's metab --version line>"
CANDIDATE_WT=$WORKTREES/metabrowser-perf-candidate
CANDIDATE_HEAD="<40-hex candidate commit>"
CANDIDATE_VERSION="<the candidate's metab --version line>"
# Optional: the condition labels the rows record (plain words), and each build's metab.
# CONTROL_LABEL=control
# CANDIDATE_LABEL=candidate
# CONTROL_METAB=$CONTROL_WT/.venv/bin/metab
# CANDIDATE_METAB=$CANDIDATE_WT/.venv/bin/metab

# ---- the harness: the checkout transitions.mjs runs from, frozen at its commit, and the
# SCENARIO_REVISION its transitions-stats.mjs must export
HARNESS_WT=$WORKTREES/metabrowser-perf-harness
HARNESS_HEAD="<40-hex harness commit>"
SCENARIO_REVISION=5
# Optional: more words for `transitions.mjs run`, split on spaces. Empty runs every journey
# in the standard regime. The driver owns --exp, --corpus, --runs, --out, --condition and
# --order, and refuses them here.
# HARNESS_ARGS="--journeys files,keyboard"

# ---- the corpus, and the provenance the first pair must start on, as provenance.mjs's
# corpusProvenance reads it: commit, trunk (origin/main) and refs digest; it must be clean
CORPUS=$WORKTREES/metabrowser-perf-corpus-v2
CORPUS_COMMIT="<40-hex corpus commit>"
CORPUS_TRUNK="<40-hex trunk commit>"
CORPUS_REFS="<16-hex refs digest>"

# ---- the series
# Stop at TARGET judged pairs, or after MAX_ATTEMPTS attempts.
TARGET=6
MAX_ATTEMPTS=20
# Pacing: a pair starts only after the one-minute load stays under MAX_LOAD for
# QUIET_SECONDS (sampled every 10 s) and no other transitions.mjs run is in progress.
MAX_LOAD=12
# Optional: the load rule's bound, passed to the load filter as --max-load.
# EXCLUDE_MAX_LOAD=12
# Optional: the load filter and the stopping count. A replacement count takes
# paced-series-count.mjs's arguments and prints its "judged N ..." last line.
# LOAD_FILTER=$WORKTREE/explorations/performance-loop/experiments/exp-060-062-load-filter.mjs
# COUNT=$WORKTREE/explorations/performance-loop/paced-series-count.mjs
# Optional: the operational stops and the pacing window.
# LOCK_WAIT_HOURS=12
# QUIET_WAIT_MINUTES=60
# QUIET_SECONDS=60
# Optional: 1 holds `caffeinate -i` while the driver runs, so the machine does not sleep
# while idle; 0 does not.
# CAFFEINATE=1
# Optional: words added to the lock's owner line, such as the round's purpose.
# OWNER_NOTE="closing round"
